    "reason": "[ev-f9d32317b49c] is the only evidence, and it is a bare changelog line saying the server now makes deep copies of objects returned by informers. It names no setting, flag, resource or operator-visible effect. The surrounding Features section adds nothing about this item. The proposed exposure is also unsound: it uses product-version, which is meant for another product's version, to test argo-cd against itself (>=3.0.0). That condition would flag every environment, and nothing shows those environments are exposed to anything. Deciding the exposure would need the PR (#22173/#22179) or upgrade-guide text that states whether the change has any operator-visible effect and under what configuration.",
